{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     search — the trigger for Ghost's own search modal.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     `data-ghost-search` is Ghost's hook: Sodo Search binds to it and opens the
     modal. There is no theme-side search to build, index or keep working, and
     it stays correct as Ghost changes.

     Shaped like a field rather than an icon because that is what NSDS's
     .ns-navsearch is — the typing happens in the modal, and a field-shaped
     button is what tells a reader that. Below lg the bar collapses it to the
     icon-only form, which is a modifier, not a second control.

     PARAMETERS
       compact   truthy → always the icon form (used in the course bar, where
                 the title needs the width)
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<button type="button"
        class="ns-navsearch{{#if compact}} ns-navsearch--icon{{/if}}"
        data-ghost-search
        aria-label="{{t "Search this site"}}">
    <i class="ph ph-magnifying-glass" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    {{#unless compact}}
        <span class="ns-navsearch__text">{{t "Search"}}</span>
        <kbd class="ns-navsearch__kbd">⌘K</kbd>
    {{/unless}}
</button>
